Z||000006||hyhy4u||08-21-2001||05:52 PM||||How about this for cool...<BR>Late 80's my dad went up to the plant in Detroit and he got to go into the building that they keep all GM's prototype cars..there crash cars..and just about every other car.  He told me a couple stories about cars he saw..he said he walked up to a caddy and looked under the hood and all he saw was a big bucket type of thing with a hole in the bottom..and my dad looks at the guy and says what the heck is this??!!. The guys said that GM made a car that could completly run off Manure..Manuer..ok..i dont know how ya spell it! Right away im like. "did ya see any fieros?????", and hes like..hmm..dont really remember, hes like..if they where somewhere thats the place they would be!..All i had to say was get me in there!, haha  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Jason-||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||08-21-2001||07:51 PM||||I attended the POCI national in Buffalo last year and one of the speakers was a Pontiac development guy.  He told the story that the 89 Fiero had a 2.9 turbo that was a lot faster than they had imagined and the Corvette guys watching the track testing had that combination canceled before the cars got back from the track.  The turbo version was faster than the 89 vette at half the cost.  Pontiac had some concern that buyers of this car would require some drivers education before let out on the road.<P>Again, just hear say.<P>I don't think Pontiac will let the 89 prototypes out of there hands, if they are even still around, so the idea of the cars making the show circuit is doubtful.||||reg||1
